## Highlights
- Pepsin-soluble collagen was extracted from mackerel (Scomber japonicus) bone and skin.
- Subcritical water was used to produce collagen hydrolysates.
- Subcritical water treatment produced low molecular weight (<1650 Da) peptides.
- The collagen hydrolysate showed high antioxidant activity.
